# frameaudit

Offline decode-frame audit and PTS repair tool for action-game replay clips.

It decodes local video files with PyAV, performs a bounded stable reorder of
decoded frames, repairs missing / duplicate / backwards / over-threshold PTS
values using rational time-base arithmetic, collects frame-type and NumPy
luminance statistics, and emits a terminal summary plus an optional per-frame
JSONL repair manifest.

## Usage

```bash
python -m frameaudit fixture --out clip.mp4 --frames 120 --fps 30 --faults 4
python -m frameaudit scan --input clip.mp4 --fps 30 --format json \
    --frames-out frames.jsonl
python -m frameaudit scan --input clips/ --format json
```

Exit codes: `0` success, `1` media processing failure, `2` parameter error,
`3` output error.
